1
00:00:02,803 --> 00:00:04,633
(Penny:)Hey, how are things going
with your parents?

2
00:00:04,638 --> 00:00:07,308
Not great.
They hired divorce attorneys.

3
00:00:07,308 --> 00:00:08,808
(Sheldon:)You know, speaking
of attorneys,

4
00:00:08,809 --> 00:00:11,209
(Sheldon:)if I ever needed
a lawyer,

5
00:00:11,212 --> 00:00:14,342
(Sheldon:)I would not hire
She-Hulk.

6
00:00:15,483 --> 00:00:17,453
(Penny:)You know what?
That was almost on topic.

7
00:00:17,451 --> 00:00:19,651
(Penny:)I'm gonna say,
"Good job, Sheldon."

8
00:00:20,588 --> 00:00:22,658
(Amy:)Wait, She-Hulk's
a lawyer?

9
00:00:22,656 --> 00:00:24,626
(Howard:)Yeah, she works at
a law firm in New York.

10
00:00:24,625 --> 00:00:27,865
(Sheldon:)Yes, but she's the only
monster at the firm.

11
00:00:27,862 --> 00:00:29,832
(Sheldon:)Between you, me
and the wall,

12
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:33,030
(Sheldon:)I think she's an
affirmative action hire.

13
00:00:34,568 --> 00:00:36,498
(Raj:)Anyway, Dad's gonna
be here in town,

14
00:00:36,504 --> 00:00:38,774
(Raj:)so I won't be able to do
Christmas dinner this year.

15
00:00:38,773 --> 00:00:40,773
(Amy:)If you're not up
to hosting Christmas dinner,

16
00:00:40,775 --> 00:00:42,205
(Amy:)I'm happy to do it.

17
00:00:42,209 --> 00:00:43,809
(Amy:)You can even
bring your father.

18
00:00:43,811 --> 00:00:45,641
(Raj:)That would be nice.

19
00:00:45,646 --> 00:00:46,646
(Amy:)I've always wanted to do

20
00:00:46,647 --> 00:00:48,377
(Amy:)a traditional
Victorian Christmas.

21
00:00:48,382 --> 00:00:51,382
Parlor games,
goose and figgy pudding...

22
00:00:51,385 --> 00:00:53,755
Ugh!

23
00:00:53,754 --> 00:00:55,654
(Sheldon:)English pudding.

24
00:00:55,656 --> 00:00:57,356
Y-You get yourself all
excited for pudding,

25
00:00:57,358 --> 00:01:00,228
(Sheldon:)and here comes a cake
with raisins in it.

26
00:01:00,227 --> 00:01:01,927
(Sheldon:)I'm not going.

27
00:01:01,929 --> 00:01:03,299
(Amy:)You're going.

28
00:01:03,297 --> 00:01:05,427
(Sheldon:)Why do you hate me?

29
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:06,763
(Amy:)I don't hate you.

30
00:01:06,767 --> 00:01:07,767
(Amy:)I love you.

31
00:01:07,768 --> 00:01:09,198
(Sheldon:)Well, you call it love,

32
00:01:09,203 --> 00:01:10,933
(Sheldon:)but it has a lot
of raisins in it.

33
00:01:13,641 --> 00:01:15,611
(Raj:)Amy, good luck getting
these guys excited

34
00:01:15,609 --> 00:01:16,709
(Raj:)about a dinner
with a theme.

35
00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:20,280
(Raj:)I gave up when no one cared
about my Tom Hanks-giving.

36
00:01:21,582 --> 00:01:24,612
(Bernadette:)I think a Victorian Christmas
sounds nice.

37
00:01:24,618 --> 00:01:25,418
(Howard:)I agree.
Why not?

38
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:26,589
(Penny:)Me, too.

39
00:01:26,587 --> 00:01:28,587
You guys suck!

40
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:32,259
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

